"""Affine potential pieces and chosen descent occurrences of the typed class-A carrier of the minus line (n+1,n,n-1).

Generated from exact complete seed graphs n=8..24 (BFS first-hit depths, with
potential X = a n + b j + c satisfying depth = floor(X/3) on each piece), then
verified symbolically for every n>=8 by `psc.class_a_carrier_descent`. The
tables are a proof *target*; nothing here is evidence until that verifier
accepts every row. Regenerate with oracles/python/class_a_descent_table.py.

Carrier row(s) 99 admit no exact fit (the first-hit plateaus shift with n mod 3);
there the potential only satisfies depth <= floor(X/3) <= depth + 1.
"""


